{"content":[{"c":["REHOBOTH-IR"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["Name meaning “broad places of the city.” It was the second city built by Nimrod the hunter (",{"c":["kjv"],"sourceClass":"sc","t":"span"}," “Asshur”) in Assyria (",{"href":"?bref=Gen.10.11","r":"Gen.10.11","rawR":"Gen.10.11","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Gen.10.11","value":"Gen.10.11"}],"t":"ref","v":"Gn 10:11"},"; ",{"c":["kjv"],"sourceClass":"sc","t":"span"}," “Rehoboth”). Opinion differs as to whether it was a distinct municipality (a suburb of Nineveh) or, since the name of the town is not mentioned in Assyrian literature, open squares or broad streets within Nineveh itself."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"RehobothIr","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Gn 10:11","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Gen.10.11","rawQueryValue":"Gen.10.11","sourceRefExact":"Gen.10.11"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"b583e38cffd3231f82f2ce7b0f908dc71e345e30ab1b701ed49b4f8b0a402122","sourceItemName":"RehobothIr","sourceItemOrder":97,"sourceMember":"Articles/R.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"RehobothIr","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Rehoboth-Ir","title":"Rehoboth-Ir","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}